From 2cdb5a290568d643e0b92db124e0df554365ce9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:17:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/39] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: add the PCIe power domain

The PCIe controller has no power-domains property, so genpd treats
PD_PCIE as unused. When the last known consumer of the PCK-600 binds,
sync_state powers the domain off under the running NVMe drive and all
CPUs stall. This appeared when the display driver was loaded.

The vendor device tree links pcie@6000000 to this domain. Do the same.

Tested on an OrangePi 4 Pro: the display driver loads, and NVMe stays
available.

Made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 164f158db..e7fb44fce 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -526,6 +526,7 @@ pcie: pcie@6000000 {
 
 			#interrupt-cells = <1>;
 
+			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_PCIE>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			pcie_intc: legacy-interrupt-controller {
